From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.mediacontrol: The transport controls as an MPRIS player (6523)

An enabled SystemMediaTransportControls session is now published on the
user's own session bus as org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.<program>.instance<pid>_<n>.
It carries the display updater's title, artist, album, album artist,
track number and cover (written to $XDG_CACHE_HOME/stained-glass/mpris,
0700), PlaybackStatus, LoopStatus, Shuffle, Rate and Position, and
CanPlay/CanPause/CanGoNext/CanGoPrevious from the IsXEnabled flags. Every
change sends PropertiesChanged. Play, Pause, PlayPause, Stop, Next and
Previous from the bus come back as ButtonPressed, from a thread of the
controls. A button the program has not enabled does nothing. libdbus is
loaded at run time by a unixlib. Without it, or without a session bus
(none is ever autolaunched), nothing changes. Nothing is system-wide and
nothing goes to the network.

windows.storage: a RandomAccessStreamReference over another
implementation's stream (shcore's COM-stream wrapper, a managed stream)
could not be opened (E_NOINTERFACE). Its bytes are now read into a
snapshot, as for our own streams.
---
